	sh:targetClass dd:ProjectDocument .
dd:ProjectFact a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "One fact about a project that a check agent proposes and a person confirms: a funder, a repository a funder or institution requires, whether a file is deposited, whether a sensitive field or file may be published and at what precision, the licence, an output a data management plan committed to share, a standard, vocabulary or format the researcher chose for the dataset, which attached document is the project's data management plan, or what data the project collects and how (docs/specs/projects.md). fact_kind says which of the value slots apply; fact_subject is the key a person's decision counts by, so the last decision on a subject stands. An agent's payload carries proposals in proposed_facts; only a person's decision makes one a fact, and the conductor gives the facts a person decided to every drafter and orchestrator in the project as project_decisions, without proposed_because." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n453 ;
	sh:property _:c14n118 , _:c14n123 , _:c14n135 , _:c14n142 , _:c14n143 , _:c14n150 , _:c14n190 , _:c14n193 , _:c14n203 , _:c14n232 , _:c14n233 , _:c14n299 , _:c14n334 , _:c14n355 , _:c14n414 , _:c14n434 , _:c14n464 , _:c14n466 , _:c14n472 , _:c14n490 , _:c14n498 , _:c14n504 , _:c14n507 , _:c14n510 , _:c14n523 , _:c14n550 , _:c14n581 , _:c14n582 , _:c14n593 , _:c14n70 , _:c14n86 ;
	sh:targetClass dd:ProjectFact .
dd:ProposesFacts a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Mixed into an agent's payload class when the agent proposes project facts for a person to confirm (docs/specs/projects.md). The harness reads proposed_facts by this name and never needs to know the payload class." ;
	sh:closed false ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n586 ;
	sh:property _:c14n390 ;
	sh:targetClass dd:ProposesFacts .
dd:Question a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "One question a conversational agent asks the researcher in its reply, shown as a form field and answered with the reply's other questions in the next turn. A choice question has a fixed set of options, of which one or several may be chosen, and where question_other is true the researcher may answer in their own words instead; option values are unique within the question. A short or long text question is answered in the researcher's own words and has no options; a short text question may suggest answers (question_suggestions), which the researcher may take or ignore. Asking never suspends the run: the researcher may skip a question, or ignore them all and type (docs/specs/orchestration.md)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n183 ;
	sh:property _:c14n10 , _:c14n231 , _:c14n246 , _:c14n321 , _:c14n370 , _:c14n376 , _:c14n585 , _:c14n6 ;
	sh:targetClass dd:Question .
dd:QuestionAnswer a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "The researcher's answer to one question of a reply, named by its question_key: the values of the options chosen, for a choice question, and the answer in their own words, for a text question or where a choice question allows it." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n248 ;
	sh:property _:c14n14 , _:c14n236 , _:c14n377 ;
	sh:targetClass dd:QuestionAnswer .
dd:Reply a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "The payload of a conversational agent: the text of its reply. An orchestrator's reply is grounded on its input and on the envelopes of the invocations it delegated to. An orchestrator may propose a data description fact from what the researcher said, for a person to confirm (docs/specs/orchestration.md)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
